<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE refentry PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook V4.1.2//EN"
  "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.1.2/docbookx.dtd">

<!-- $Id$ -->

<refentry id="gfarm-prun.1">

<refentryinfo><date>10 Nov 2026</date></refentryinfo>

<refmeta>
<refentrytitle>gfarm-prun</refentrytitle>
<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
<refmiscinfo>Gfarm</refmiscinfo>
</refmeta>

<refnamediv id="name">
<refname>gfarm-prun</refname>
<refpurpose>execute a command on multiple hosts</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv id="synopsis">
<cmdsynopsis sepchar=" ">
  <command moreinfo="none">gfarm-prun</command>
    <arg choice="opt" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>options</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="plain" rep="norepeat"><replaceable>command</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="opt" rep="repeat"><replaceable>arg</replaceable></arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<!-- body begins here -->

<refsect1 id="description"><title>DESCRIPTION</title>
<para><command moreinfo="none">gfarm-prun</command> executes
<parameter moreinfo="none">command</parameter> with
<parameter moreinfo="none">arg</parameter>s on each host listed in
a hostfile, by using a remote shell command,
<command moreinfo="none">ssh</command> by default.
It is useful, for example, to set up or manage filesystem nodes of
Gfarm.</para>

<para>By default, the command is executed on one host after another.
When the -p option is specified, the command is executed on multiple
hosts in parallel.</para>

<para>The hostfile has one host name in each line.  Only the first
field of each line is used.  Characters from `#' to the end of the
line are regarded as a comment, and empty lines are ignored.
The default hostfile is <filename moreinfo="none">$HOME/.nodelist</filename>.</para>

<para>The local host is skipped unless the -a option is specified.
A host is regarded as the local host when its name matches the
output of <command moreinfo="none">hostname</command> or one of the
IP addresses displayed by <command moreinfo="none">hostname -I</command>.
A host name also matches when only one of them has the domain part,
for example, <literal>node1</literal> and <literal>node1.example.com</literal>,
but <literal>node1</literal> does not match <literal>node10</literal>.
These names can be changed by the PRUN_HOSTNAME environment
variable.</para>

<para>The command line is passed to the remote shell command, thus it
is interpreted by a shell on the remote host.  Wildcards in the command
line are expanded on the remote host, not on the local host.</para>

<para>Unless the -stdin option is specified, the standard input of the
remote command is
<filename moreinfo="none">/dev/null</filename>.</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="options"><title>OPTIONS</title>
<variablelist>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-a</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Executes the command also on the local host, if it is listed in
the hostfile.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-h</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">hostfile</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a hostfile.  If `-' is specified, the list of hosts is
read from the standard input.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-m</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">max_jobs</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies the maximum number of hosts on which the command is
executed in parallel with the -p option.  The default is 16.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-n</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Displays the commands that would be executed, but does not
execute them.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-p</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Executes the command on multiple hosts in parallel in the
background.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-rsh</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">rsh_command</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a remote shell command.  The default is
<command moreinfo="none">ssh</command>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-stdin</option> <parameter moreinfo="none">file</parameter></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a file that is given to the standard input of the
command on each host.  This option can be specified multiple times.
In this case, the files are concatenated.  If `-' is specified, the
standard input of <command moreinfo="none">gfarm-prun</command> is
read once, and it is given to the command on each host.  `-' cannot be
specified for both the -h option and the -stdin option.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><option>-v</option></term>
<listitem>
<para>Displays the host name before executing the command on the host.
This option has no effect with the -p option.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="environment-variables"><title>ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES</title>
<variablelist>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_RSH</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a remote shell command.  The default is
<command moreinfo="none">ssh</command>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_HOSTFILE</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies a hostfile.  The default is
<filename moreinfo="none">$HOME/.nodelist</filename>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_HOSTNAME</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies the names of the local host, separated by spaces.
The default is the output of <command moreinfo="none">hostname</command>
and <command moreinfo="none">hostname -I</command>.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_MAX_JOBS</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>Specifies the maximum number of parallel jobs.  The default is
16.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_PARALLEL</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>If it is set to <literal>yes</literal>, the command is executed
in parallel as with the -p option.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_ALL_INCLUDE_MYSELF</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>If it is set to <literal>yes</literal>, the command is executed
also on the local host as with the -a option.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><envar>PRUN_VERBOSE</envar></term>
<listitem>
<para>If it is set to <literal>yes</literal>, the host name is
displayed as with the -v option.</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="exit-status"><title>EXIT STATUS</title>
<para><command moreinfo="none">gfarm-prun</command> exits with 0 when
the command succeeds on all hosts.  Otherwise, it exits with the exit
status of the remote shell command for a host on which the command
fails.  When it fails on two or more hosts, the exit status for one of
them is returned.</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="examples"><title>EXAMPLES</title>
<para>Displays the uptime of all hosts listed in
<filename moreinfo="none">$HOME/.nodelist</filename>,
except the local host.</para>
<literallayout format="linespecific" class="normal">
	$ gfarm-prun -v uptime
</literallayout>

<para>Restarts gfsd on all hosts listed in
<filename moreinfo="none">hosts</filename>, in parallel.</para>
<literallayout format="linespecific" class="normal">
	$ gfarm-prun -p -h hosts sudo systemctl restart gfsd
</literallayout>

<para>Executes a local shell script
<filename moreinfo="none">setup.sh</filename> on each host.</para>
<literallayout format="linespecific" class="normal">
	$ gfarm-prun -h hosts -stdin setup.sh sh
</literallayout>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="files"><title>FILES</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><filename moreinfo="none">$HOME/.nodelist</filename></term>
<listitem>
<para>the default hostfile</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1 id="see-also"><title>SEE ALSO</title>
<para>
  <citerefentry>
  <refentrytitle>gfarm-pcp</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
  </citerefentry>,
  <citerefentry>
  <refentrytitle>ssh</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
  </citerefentry>
</para>
</refsect1>

</refentry>
